    "id": "global-voices-women-capulana-dresses-and-police-violence-stand-out-at-nampula-protests",
    "title": "Mozambique: Women, capulana dresses, and police violence stand out at Nampula protests",
    "deck": "Women in Nampula turned the capulana into a symbol of resistance, while social media amplified protests, digital activism, and debates regarding state control and civic rights in Mozambique.",
    "source": "Global Voices",
    "sourceId": "global-voices",
    "sourceUrl": "https://globalvoices.org/2026/08/25/mozambique-women-capulana-dresses-and-police-violence-stand-out-at-nampula-protests/",
    "sourceFeed": "https://globalvoices.org/feed/?cat=-28",
    "category": "生活",
    "topic": "Citizen Media · Digital Activism · Governance",
    "publishedAt": "2026-08-25",
    "license": "Global Voices original text is licensed under Creative Commons Attribution 3.0 (CC BY 3.0).",
    "attribution": "Text: Liam Anderson · Originally published by Global Voices · Plain-text adaptation: Leafbound",
    "contentNote": "只匯入 Global Voices 原創文章的英文純文字改編；外部內容共享稿、圖片、圖說、影音、長篇引文與括號內非英文原文拼寫均不複製。",
    "minutes": 4,
